   greedy on 250 covering families: reached >=14/183 in 148, below in 102
=> equioscillation (>=2 binding runners at t*=a/q*) is the de la Vallee-Poussin lower-bound structure;
   greedy Stern-Brocot (AAA-style) finds t* when it doesn't stick in a local max => the certificate is
   a RATIONAL t* whose CF convergents are the binding denominators.
